        {
          "entry_id": 2858,
          "chunk_index": 1,
          "similarity_score": 0.35030246,
          "considered": true,
          "chunk_text": "# Procedure codes and self-pay prices\n## Medical procedures\n\n- 93000: resting 12-lead electrocardiogram, with the doctor's reading of it - $65\n- 94010: spirometry - $85\n- 93784: 24-hour ambulatory blood pressure monitoring - $140\n- 81002: urine dipstick test done in the clinic - $15\n- 69210: ear wax removal, per ear - $75\n- 17110: wart freezing (cryotherapy), up to 14 warts in one session - $90",
          "text_truncated": false
        },
        {
          "entry_id": 2858,
          "chunk_index": 2,
          "similarity_score": 0.30579042,
          "considered": true,
          "chunk_text": "# Procedure codes and self-pay prices\n## Dental procedures\n\n- D2391: tooth-coloured filling on one surface of a back tooth - $210\n- D2140: silver (amalgam) filling on one surface - $160\n- D7140: simple tooth extraction - $240",
          "text_truncated": false
        },
        {
          "entry_id": 2845,
          "chunk_index": 0,
          "similarity_score": 0.26671466,
          "considered": true,
          "chunk_text": "Question: How much will my visit cost if I am paying out-of-pocket?\nAnswer: Out-of-pocket rates are $120 for a General Practitioner (GP) visit, $180 for a Dentist appointment, and $160 for all other specialist consultations.",
          "text_truncated": false
        },
        {
          "entry_id": 2852,
          "chunk_index": 4,
          "similarity_score": 0.253404,
          "considered": true,
          "chunk_text": "# Vaccinations\n## Self-pay vaccine prices\n\nIf your insurance does not cover a vaccine, these are the self-pay prices: flu vaccine $35, high-dose flu vaccine $70, Tdap $55, hepatitis A $85 per dose, typhoid injection $90, oral typhoid course $95, hepatitis B $70 per dose. They are the price of the vaccine itself, and are charged in addition to the rate for the visit.",
          "text_truncated": false
        },
        {
          "entry_id": 2858,
          "chunk_index": 3,
          "similarity_score": 0.22021697,
          "considered": true,
          "chunk_text": "# Procedure codes and self-pay prices\n## A code you do not recognise\n\nIf your receipt shows a code that is not in this list, the front desk can tell you what it is.",
          "text_truncated": false
        },
        {
          "entry_id": 2858,
          "chunk_index": 0,
          "similarity_score": 0.21588632,
          "considered": false,
          "chunk_text": "# Procedure codes and self-pay prices\n\nYour itemized receipt lists each procedure done at your visit by its billing code. Medical procedures use five-digit CPT codes, and dental procedures use CDT cod",
          "text_truncated": true
        },
        {
          "entry_id": 2849,
          "chunk_index": 6,
          "similarity_score": 0.19046092,
          "considered": false,
          "chunk_text": "# Insurance plan guide\n## Copays and deductibles\n\nYour plan decides how much you pay at the visit. A copay is a fixed amount your plan sets for each visit, and it is collected when you check in. If yo",
          "text_truncated": true
        },
        {
          "entry_id": 2844,
          "chunk_index": 0,
          "similarity_score": 0.14935544,
          "considered": false,
          "chunk_text": "Question: What should I do if my insurance isn't listed or I am out-of-network?\nAnswer: You can pay out-of-pocket for your visit, and we can provide you with an itemized receipt to submit to your insu",
          "text_truncated": true
        },
        {
          "entry_id": 2849,
          "chunk_index": 0,
          "similarity_score": 0.114678666,
          "considered": false,
          "chunk_text": "# Insurance plan guide\n\nThis guide lists, plan by plan, the health insurance plans we are in-network with. Insurance companies sell many plans under one brand name, and being in-network with a company",
          "text_truncated": true
        },
        {
          "entry_id": 2846,
          "chunk_index": 0,
          "similarity_score": 0.10500641,
          "considered": false,
          "chunk_text": "Question: When is payment due, and what payment methods do you accept?\nAnswer: Payment is due at the time of service. We accept cash, major credit and debit cards (Visa, Mastercard, American Express),",
          "text_truncated": true
        },
        {
          "entry_id": 2843,
          "chunk_index": 0,
          "similarity_score": 0.10485712,
          "considered": false,
          "chunk_text": "Question: Which health insurance plans do you accept?\nAnswer: We accept most major insurance providers, including Blue Cross Blue Shield, Aetna, Cigna, UnitedHealthcare, and Medicare. If you're unsure",
          "text_truncated": true
        },
        {
          "entry_id": 2852,
          "chunk_index": 1,
          "similarity_score": 0.09758103,
          "considered": false,
          "chunk_text": "# Vaccinations\n## COVID-19 vaccine\n\nWe offer the updated COVID-19 vaccine for the current season made by Pfizer-BioNTech (Comirnaty). We do not stock the Moderna (Spikevax) or Novavax vaccines.",
          "text_truncated": false
        },
        {
          "entry_id": 2847,
          "chunk_index": 0,
          "similarity_score": 0.08927351,
          "considered": false,
          "chunk_text": "Question: What are your clinic hours and locations?\nAnswer: We are open Monday through Saturday from 9:00 AM to 6:00 PM at 15a Willson St. The nearest free parking is a 3-minute walk away at the Mega ",
          "text_truncated": true
        },
        {
          "entry_id": 2849,
          "chunk_index": 5,
          "similarity_score": 0.08626907,
          "considered": false,
          "chunk_text": "# Insurance plan guide\n## Medicare and Medicaid\n\nWe accept Original Medicare (Part B) for medical visits. Medicare does not cover routine dental care, so dental appointments are self-pay for Medicare ",
          "text_truncated": true
        },
        {
          "entry_id": 2849,
          "chunk_index": 7,
          "similarity_score": 0.084478654,
          "considered": false,
          "chunk_text": "# Insurance plan guide\n## Updating your insurance\n\nIf your insurance has changed since your last visit, tell the front desk at check-in and fill in Form IC-2, the Insurance Update Form, so the claim g",
          "text_truncated": true
        },
        {
          "entry_id": 2852,
          "chunk_index": 2,
          "similarity_score": 0.08021,
          "considered": false,
          "chunk_text": "# Vaccinations\n## Tetanus, diphtheria and whooping cough (Tdap)\n\nAdults need a tetanus booster every 10 years. We use Boostrix, which also protects against diphtheria and whooping cough (pertussis).",
          "text_truncated": false
        },
        {
          "entry_id": 2851,
          "chunk_index": 1,
          "similarity_score": 0.07989812,
          "considered": false,
          "chunk_text": "# Preparing for tests at the clinic\n## Electrocardiogram (ECG)\n\nA resting 12-lead ECG records the electrical activity of your heart through ten small sticky electrodes placed on your chest, arms and l",
          "text_truncated": true
        },
        {
          "entry_id": 2849,
          "chunk_index": 3,
          "similarity_score": 0.07966727,
          "considered": false,
          "chunk_text": "# Insurance plan guide\n## Cigna\n\nWe are in-network with Cigna Open Access Plus (OAP) and Cigna PPO plans. Cigna LocalPlus plans are in-network only for members who live in our county; the network area",
          "text_truncated": true
        },
        {
          "entry_id": 2850,
          "chunk_index": 1,
          "similarity_score": 0.078673966,
          "considered": false,
          "chunk_text": "# Dental care guide\n## Dental insurance\n\nMedical insurance plans do not cover dental care. For dental appointments we accept these dental plans: Delta Dental PPO, MetLife PDP Plus and Guardian DentalG",
          "text_truncated": true
        },
        {
          "entry_id": 2855,
          "chunk_index": 2,
          "similarity_score": 0.07847311,
          "considered": false,
          "chunk_text": "# Checking in and registering\n## Language interpreters\n\nFree telephone interpreting is available in more than 200 languages for any appointment. Ask for it when you book or when you check in; there is",
          "text_truncated": true
        },
        {
          "entry_id": 2857,
          "chunk_index": 0,
          "similarity_score": 0.07720543,
          "considered": false,
          "chunk_text": "# General practice services\n## Annual physical examination\n\nAn annual physical is a preventive check-up for adults who feel well. It includes a review of your medical history and current medicines; yo",
          "text_truncated": true
        },
        {
          "entry_id": 2855,
          "chunk_index": 0,
          "similarity_score": 0.0730046,
          "considered": false,
          "chunk_text": "# Checking in and registering\n## Registering as a new patient\n\nNew patients fill in three forms at their first visit:\n\n- Form PR-1, New Patient Registration: your contact details, emergency contact an",
          "text_truncated": true
        },
        {
          "entry_id": 2855,
          "chunk_index": 3,
          "similarity_score": 0.07239218,
          "considered": false,
          "chunk_text": "# Checking in and registering\n## Bringing someone with you\n\nYou may bring one adult companion into the consulting room. Anyone else who comes with you can wait in the waiting area.",
          "text_truncated": false
        },
        {
          "entry_id": 2849,
          "chunk_index": 1,
          "similarity_score": 0.07123913,
          "considered": false,
          "chunk_text": "# Insurance plan guide\n## Blue Cross Blue Shield\n\nWe are in-network with Blue Cross Blue Shield PPO plans, including BlueCard PPO members whose plan was issued in another state; look for the suitcase ",
          "text_truncated": true
        },
        {
          "entry_id": 2857,
          "chunk_index": 3,
          "similarity_score": 0.07058816,
          "considered": false,
          "chunk_text": "# General practice services\n## Minor procedures\n\nWe freeze common warts and verrucas with cryotherapy (liquid nitrogen). A wart may need two to four treatments, about three weeks apart. We do not remo",
